	/* ============================================================= *
	 * SPECIALISATIES — the two-discipline photographic diptych (D-20 asymmetry, D-23 all-dark)
	 *
	 * VARIATION EXPRESSION #2 (P4.7): "two light sources". The elevation here is NOT the .work room and NOT a
	 * gold seam — it is a DIFFERENT expression of the same "photography is the light source" principle: each of
	 * the two discipline photographs appears to cast its OWN light into the surrounding dark. A cool pool sits
	 * upper-left, under/around the architecture plate (which is itself a cool blue-sky image); a warm pool sits
	 * lower-right, under/around the interior plate (a warm artificial-light image). Together they read as a
	 * cool→warm chromatic diagonal that literally maps the two disciplines — "twee disciplines, één benadering"
	 * expressed in light. This makes the chapter MEDIUM intensity (photography-led, richer than the flat base,
	 * quieter than .work's full-bleed plate) and keeps gold's structural-LINE role exclusive to .work (this
	 * chapter carries no added gold line — anti-repetition). A `::before` (z-index:-1, contained by isolation)
	 * so it paints above the section fill but below every card; each photo's opaque frame covers the peak, so the
